<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  RUT_HolyFlamePrecepts.xml          UtinniPatches — SUMP_UTINNI_LAYER_1 §2

  "The holy act": flame statuary as worship of the evil sun god, Sh'kaar the
  All-Searing (design/Jawa/divine_satiation_engine.md §8). Statues/worship
  split ruled by card: statues RM-tier secular (RM_FlameStatuary,
  SUMP_GASLIGHT_1); the ritual/holy meaning is this Utinni-tier precept.

  Shape copied from this repo's own RUT_FungusEating.xml precedent (issue/
  label/description/impact/displayOrderInIssue, plus a PreceptComp_
  SelfTookMemoryThought comp — real vanilla class, RimWorld/PreceptComp_
  SelfTookMemoryThought.cs decompiled and read in full). eventDef/thought
  reference RUT_HolyFlameEvents.xml/RUT_HolyFlameThoughts.xml, both defined
  alongside this file under the same MayRequire, so there is no cross-mod
  resolve risk.

  🔑 REACHABILITY: a PreceptDef is only ever selectable if some MemeDef's
  <requireOne> names it (RimWorld/MemeDef.cs: requireOne is a
  List<List<PreceptDef>> — there is no issue-level "just show every precept
  under this issue" fallback, confirmed reading the class). Shipping this
  PreceptDef alone would be silently unreachable content — the exact "zero
  rows is a failure, not a footnote" trap. Patches/HolyFlame_
  RitualistWiring.xml appends a new requireOne GROUP containing this one
  precept onto the vanilla Anomaly meme `Ritualist` (thematically the closest
  fit: an ideoligion that cares about ritual observance), making this precept
  selectable by ANY ideoligion — player-authored or NPC-generated — that
  picks that meme. It is NOT wired into the campaign's own saved ideoligion
  ("The Salvation", src/Jawa/ideoligion/The Salvation.rid): a saved .rid is
  Scribe output baked at world creation, and the only way to add a precept to
  an ALREADY-BAKED live Ideo is the in-game dev-mode ideo editor — a live,
  manual action outside this item's offline/no-bridge scope. Flagged, not
  guessed.

  No "don't care" neutral position authored (unlike FungusEating's 2-3
  positions): this is a brand new issue with exactly one meaningful stance,
  not a rebalance of a multi-position vanilla issue.
-->
<Defs>

  <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
    <defName>RUT_HolyFlame_Revered</defName>
    <issue>RUT_HolyFlame</issue>
    <label>revered</label>
    <description>The flame that issues from carved stone is Sh'kaar's own signature: worked stone the sun agreed to speak through. Standing before it and giving it its due is the holy act.</description>
    <impact>Medium</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>1</displayOrderInIssue>
    <comps>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SelfTookMemoryThought">
        <eventDef>RUT_PerformedHolyFlameAct</eventDef>
        <thought>RUT_PerformedHolyFlameAct</thought>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </PreceptDef>

</Defs>
